# General architecture

Dependency direction is one way: screen → component → hook → service → infrastructure. A lower layer never imports a component, a hook, or a screen.

| Layer | Does | Must not |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Screen | Compose the route. Loading and error for the route. | Call `fetch` or the database. |
| Component | Render props. Handle input. | Hold business rules or global server state. |
| Hook | Orchestrate queries, mutations, and UI state. | Build SQL or HTTP details. |
| Service | Business rules. Depend on interfaces. | Import UI. |
| Infrastructure | API, database, files. | Contain product rules. |

Resolve services from the project container. Do not `new ConcreteService()` in a screen, component, or hook, and do not import a concrete service into those layers.

A feature keeps its components, hooks, and helpers private. Another feature imports the public service or the shared layer, not an internal file.

One module, one reason to change. Extend with configuration and interfaces. Mocks must satisfy the same contract as production. Prefer a small interface over one that forces unused methods. Split a file that fetches, validates, and renders.

Build a feature in this order: types and Zod schema, service interface and implementation, endpoint, hook, components, screen.
